"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: pin the software `raster` text lane (`fb_text_ttf_aa_clip_range_adv`
-> `_ttf_rasterize_glyph` in paint_gradients_text) to Chrome 159's font-cache
-key size. Chrome rasterises a fractional `font-size` at
`trunc(trunc_f32(S * 100) / 100 * 64) / 64` px (font_cache_key_size_chrome159
_spec), so every size that keys to the same 26.6 value paints the same pixels.
The raster lane handed the hinted outline the raw milli size instead (18720 vs
18715), so 18.715 / 18.718 / 18.72 px drew different glyphs.
Audience: web renderer text raster maintainers.

Chrome oracle (Chrome for Testing 159, `--headless=new --disable-gpu
--hide-scrollbars --force-device-scale-factor=1 --window-size=400,300
--screenshot`, sans-serif = Liberation Sans): page `_page(S)` below, gray text
(`opacity:0.99`) and LCD text (no opacity) captured separately. PNG md5:

| S       | gray (opacity .99)  | LCD               | key (1/64 px) |
|---------|---------------------|-------------------|---------------|
| 18.715  | 905f4828...         | d06c141e...       | 1197          |
| 18.718  | 905f4828...         | d06c141e...       | 1197          |
| 18.72   | 905f4828...         | d06c141e...       | 1197          |
| 18.7205 | 5abe13e0...         | ac3debd7...       | 1198          |
| 18.71   | f176d005...         | 9d7dff93...       | 1196          |

Chrome paints 18.715, 18.718 and 18.72 byte-identically. Before this fix the
raster lane differed from its own 18.72 frame by 32 px at 18.715 and 7 px at
18.718 (400x30 frame).
Resolution: the software raster lane has no device-scale entry
(`simple_web_layout_render_html_software_pixels` is 1x only), so this spec runs
at the lane's only resolution; the same 1x TTF (Liberation Sans) is on both
sides. The k=4 lanes take their size from the same
`sfnt_font_cache_key_size_26_6` via font_renderer.
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-BROWSER-ENGINE-FRACTIONAL-FONT-SIZE-001 -- the raster text lane rasterises at Chrome's font-cache-key size.
"""
# @tag: unit, browser_engine, text, raster, chrome159
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_paint_gradients_text.spl 1%
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer.{simple_web_layout_render_html_software_pixels}

val RW: i32 = 400
val RH: i32 = 30

fn _page(size: text) -> text:
    "<!doctype html><html><body style=\"margin:0;background:#fff\"><div style=\"position:absolute;left:4px;top:0;opacity:0.99;font:" + size + "px sans-serif;color:#000;line-height:30px\">Examplesshowapqmoceasd</div></body></html>"

# Pixels of `a` that differ from `b` in any channel.
fn _diff_px(a: [u32], b: [u32]) -> i32:
    if a.len() != b.len():
        return 0 - 1
    var n = 0
    var i = 0
    while i < a.len():
        if (a[i] & 0xFFFFFFu32) != (b[i] & 0xFFFFFFu32):
            n = n + 1
        i = i + 1
    n

describe "raster text lane at Chrome's font-cache-key size (Chrome 159)":
    it "AC-1: 18.715px and 18.718px paint the same pixels as 18.72px":
        step("Chrome keys all three to 1197/64 px and paints them byte-identically")
        val at_1872 = simple_web_layout_render_html_software_pixels(_page("18.72"), RW, RH)
        val at_18715 = simple_web_layout_render_html_software_pixels(_page("18.715"), RW, RH)
        val at_18718 = simple_web_layout_render_html_software_pixels(_page("18.718"), RW, RH)
        expect(at_1872.len()).to_equal(RW * RH)
        expect(_diff_px(at_18715, at_1872)).to_equal(0)
        expect(_diff_px(at_18718, at_1872)).to_equal(0)
